{
 "about": "Worksheets with a selection and the prompt's options, each with what StatsDirect must show and the exact R object it must create. Both StatsDirect for Windows and for Mac test their own import against every case: the object must be identical() in R to \"expect.r\", evaluated with base R only. See RULES.md, which these encode.",
 "version": 1,
 "schema": {
  "cells": "A1 reference to stored cell. {\"number\": \"<decimal text, parsed to the nearest double>\"}; {\"text\": \"<string>\"}; {\"textUnits\": [<UTF-16 code units, for text JSON cannot carry, e.g. a lone surrogate>]}; {\"boolean\": true|false}; {\"error\": \"#DIV/0!\"}; {\"date\"|\"datetime\"|\"time\"|\"duration\": \"<1900-system serial, decimal text>\", \"format\": \"<number format>\"}; {\"formula\": \"<Excel formula>\", \"value\": <stored cell of its current value>}. A cell not listed is blank.",
  "formatOnly": "cells with formatting (a number format) and no value",
  "merged": "merged areas; only the top-left cell holds a value",
  "select": "{\"entire\": true} | {\"range\": \"B2:D3\"} | {\"columns\": [\"A\", \"C\"]} | {\"rows\": [\"2:6\"]} | {\"areas\": [\"A1:A2\", \"C1:C2\"]} | {\"all\": true} (select all) | {\"none\": true} (no selection; on Windows the active cell A1)",
  "options": "\"format\": \"data frame\" | \"list\"; \"headings\": null (leave the suggestion) | true | false; \"friendly\": true | false. The data choice is the one the select names (Entire worksheet for \"entire\", Selected cells otherwise).",
  "expect": "\"entire\" and \"selected\": the two data-choice labels, exactly, where given (an object gives one per platform); \"entireEnabled\", \"selectedEnabled\", \"headingsEnabled\": where given; \"headingsSuggested\": the first check box's suggestion; \"comments\": lines the script must contain; \"r\": the R expression the object must be identical() to, or null when nothing is imported; \"refusedNaming\": the import is refused with a message naming that cell, and \"refusedMessage\" gives that message exactly; \"labelsOnly\": only the labels are checked.",
  "sheet": "every case uses one worksheet named \"Sheet1\"",
  "skip": "{\"windows\"|\"mac\": \"<reason>\"}: a case that platform cannot build, with the reason; it runs on the other"
 },
 "cases": [
  {
   "name": "Entire worksheet: margins and formatting-only cells are left out",
   "rules": [
    "2.1",
    "4.1",
    "1.3",
    "5.5"
   ],
   "cells": {
    "A1": {
     "text": "Before visit"
    },
    "A2": {
     "number": "15"
    },
    "B1": {
     "text": "Group / label"
    },
    "B2": {
     "text": "café, \"quoted\"%"
    },
    "B3": {
     "text": "%NA"
    },
    "C1": {
     "text": "Outside selection"
    },
    "C2": {
     "number": "30"
    },
    "C4": {
     "number": "999"
    }
   },
   "select": {
    "entire": true
   },
   "options": {
    "format": "data frame",
    "headings": null,
    "friendly": false
   },
   "expect": {
    "entire": "Entire worksheet — A1:C4 (4 rows × 3 columns)",
    "headingsSuggested": true,
    "comments": [
     "# Data copied from the worksheet “Sheet1”, A1:C4.",
     "# Blank cells, missing-value markers and spreadsheet errors are NA."
    ],
    "r": "structure(list(c(15, NA, NA), c(\"caf\\u00e9, \\\"quoted\\\"%\", \"%NA\", NA), c(30, NA, 999)), names = c(\"Before visit\", \"Group / label\", \"Outside selection\"), row.names = c(NA_integer_, -3L), class = \"data.frame\")"
   },
   "formatOnly": [
    "H20",
    "A6"
   ]
  },
